      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-19733",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/60/605d1e0eaddf57fc624dce6fb1e0b46e7585aa735f258ca5185fa20443d5e7b9.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed between the line $3x - 4y = 0$ and the $y$-axis from $y = 0$ to $y = 3$, as shown in the picture. Given that cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis are isosceles right triangles with the hypotenuse lying on the $xy$-plane, calculate the volume of the solid.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
