      ":question/problem": "![](images/ca/ca567be33daed11ab63098d39b4dfb965662b32cbc5b1e061c308e70e8054b34.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed between the curve $x =-\\sqrt{1 - y^{2}}$ and the $y$-axis for $-1 \\le y \\le 1$, as shown in picture. If cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis are equilateral triangles, which of the following gives the volume of the solid?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
